1. DEFINITIONS
======================================================================

"Academic & Non-Profit Use" means use solely for non-commercial
academic, scientific, research, or educational purposes by:

- accredited universities, schools, and educational institutions;
- public, governmental, or non-profit research organizations; or
- individual researchers acting in a non-commercial capacity,

provided that the use is not performed by, for, or on behalf of a
for-profit entity and is not intended to provide a direct or indirect
commercial advantage to a for-profit entity.

Normal tuition, scholarships, academic salaries, non-profit grants,
charitable donations, public research funding, and reasonable
cost-recovery by a qualifying non-profit institution do not, by
themselves, make a use Commercial Use.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Covered Materials by, for, or on
behalf of a for-profit entity, or any use intended to support revenue
generation, commercial products or services, competitive commercial
advantage, internal commercial research and development, or planned
commercialization.

Commercial Use includes, without limitation:

- integration into proprietary or closed-source software;
- SaaS, API, cloud, hosted, or other commercial deployment;
- use in a commercial product, service, platform, workflow, or offering;
- internal R&D, benchmarking, validation, or product development within
  or for a for-profit organization;
- paid consulting, contract research, or professional services;
- work funded or commissioned by a for-profit entity for its commercial
  benefit;
- venture-backed, investor-funded, or otherwise commercially financed
  development intended for commercialization; and
- commercial AI or machine-learning training, fine-tuning, evaluation,
  or product development using the Covered Materials.

Mere reading, independent scientific discussion, or citation of publicly
available research descriptions, where copyright permission is not
otherwise required, is not restricted by this License.

